  "name": "proto-dumping-ground",
  "description": "A research workspace aggregating prototype implementations of high-performance Byzantine fault-tolerant consensus protocols, primarily focusing on DAG-based ordering and object-centric state models. It features the Morpheus protocol, which utilizes threshold cryptography and a dual-phase execution pipeline to optimize throughput across varying network conditions. The architecture employs a purely functional logic-processor pattern with content-addressed persistence for deterministic replay and verification.",
